      "math_academy_id": "q-70449",
      "sequence_position": 2,
      "problem": "The point $P$ with coordinates $(1,3)$ lies on the curve $y=f(x).$ Which of the following points must lie on $y=f(x-4)+4?$",
      "worked_solution": "The graph of $y=f(x-4)+4$  is a translation of the graph of $y=f(x)$ by $4$ units to the *right* and $4$ units up. So the $y$-coordinate increases by $4$ and the $x$-coordinate increases by $4.$\n\nWe know that the point $P(1,3)$ lies on $y=f(x).$ Therefore, the point $(1+4,3+4)=(5,7)$ must lie on $y=f(x-4)+4.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14245391/assets/d3779750f7ecf13b1f24eb10f7c0e694d784a079710771e70eb793327a6e9411.png)",
